The FASTA header template
Each record’s FASTA header comes from a template. The default is:
{seqid} [organism={organism}] [moltype=genomic DNA] {organism} {rrna_definition}
and the default for the per-marker files is:
{seqid}_{element} [organism={organism}] {organism} {product}
Edit them in the Export Data window. Each template is checked as you type, and Save template keeps it under a name, so a lab can keep one per submission style. Words in braces are filled in for each record:







Token
What it holds




{seqid}
The record’s name: the sample ID, or &lt;ID&gt;_p&lt;path&gt;_s&lt;contig&gt; when the sample gives more than one record. Keep it in every template.


{organism}
The organism name to submit (see below).


{rrna_definition}
The definition phrase, for example “18S ribosomal RNA gene, partial sequence; internal transcribed spacer 1, 5.8S ribosomal RNA gene, and internal transcribed spacer 2, complete sequence; and 28S ribosomal RNA gene, partial sequence.”


{completeness}
“complete sequence” or “partial sequence”, for the record as a whole.


{elements}
The features in order, for example 18S-ITS1-5.8S-ITS2-28S.


{length}, {n_features}, {missing}
Record length, number of features, and missing features.


{sci_name}, {taxid}
The name and NCBI taxon ID set in the Taxonomy step.


{element}, {product}
Per-marker template only: the marker (18S, ITS1, and so on) and its product name.



Any column of your mapping file works too, as {ColumnName}. The Your mapping columns chips in the Export Data window show every name you can use. You can also use metadata imported from GEOME, GBIF, or NCBI. See Sample metadata.
